            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "this new, extra, variable which is shared across 2 async functions, is not needed.\n\nAI suggestion:\n\n> Root cause is narrower than described. It's not that mapped keys generally produce an empty `typed`. For `nnoremap j gj` the first callback is `key='g', typed='j'` — non-empty — and it lands in the **`g` deferral** branch.\n> Only the *second* callback (`key='j', typed=''`) is swallowed by the `typed == ''` guard. A mapping like `j`→`<Down>` already dismisses fine; only RHSs starting with `g` are broken.\n> \n> **Why the guard can't just be reordered.** `messages.lua:505` runs `win_execute(pager, 'noautocmd norm! gg0')` to position the pager cursor — those two internal `g`s arrive at `cmd_on_key` as real keys with `typed=''`. Merely restoring\n> the pre-`a29a9130a982` grouping (`not typed_g and (typed == '' or ...)`) makes the second internal `g` dismiss the pager it just opened; `messages2 configured targets per kind` fails deterministically. That self-inflicted `gg0` is the\n> whole reason `typed == ''` was hoisted out.\n> \n> Fix: keep the guard subordinate to `typed_g`, and only arm `typed_g` when the `g` came from typed input:\n> \n> ```lua\n>   if not typed_g and (typed == '' or typed == '<MouseMove>' or typed == 'g' or key == 'g') then\n>     typed_g = typed ~= '' and (typed == 'g' or key == 'g')\n> ```\n> \n> ",
            "commit_id": "8e2f5d151761ca2e13d246ca8abae0fa9ff78dda",
            "created_at": "2026-08-23T22:37:48Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -579,11 +578,14 @@ function M.msg_history_show(entries, prev_cmd)\n end\n \n local typed_g = false\n+local from_typed_key = false",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41450#discussion_r3839784133",
